Atlas Cloud artifact signing key transition
===========================================

Date:     2026-09-13
Reason:   key rotation
User ID:  Atlas Cloud (Artifact Signing) <artifacts@runatlas.is>

Previous key: 4C2D 72FD DEF7 7A5C C4A7  D2C4 21CA 4588 DCB6 991E
New key:      4BB5 C9F5 58FB D4A0 981F  07EF 1A2D 98FB 5D03 6FC3

Atlas Cloud signs published artifacts with the new key. The new key is an
ed25519 primary key that certifies only, with an ed25519 signing subkey, and
it expires on 2028-09-12.

Both keys carry the same user ID, so this statement establishes which key is
which. It is signed by both keys: a reader who holds either key can confirm
the pair. The new public key also carries a certification made by the previous
key.

Artifacts signed before this date verify against the previous key. The
previous key stays valid and is still published, so existing detached
signatures and checksum sets need no re-signing. Artifacts signed after this
date verify against the new key.

Revocation of the previous key is a separate step. It is announced through the
same channels that publish the keys.

Both public keys are published at https://download.runatlas.is/ and in the
keys directory of the RunAtlas-is/cks-images repository.
